Why this is the midpoint
Memory:
    72 KiB at the stated maximum

Code invasion:
    one state array,
    one recorder update,
    four simple mode cases,
    one four-value settings layer

Performance value:
    up to four independent synchronized modulation loops

Workflow:
    assign mode -> choose length -> double-click -> play

Synchronization:
    common BPM boundary and clock-phase playback

No unnecessary additions:
    no file format,
    no dynamic mode insertion,
    no source-selection layer,
    no resampler object,
    no per-channel eight-track recording
This provides substantially more musical value than a single loop while avoiding the waste and global coupling of eight simultaneous channel recordings.

